        "identifier": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/blob/b6939a3a0d89e5f999fa8c6483a6ef646c1e2923/FormalConjectures/OpenQuantumProblems/35.lean",
        "note": "Supplies the statements `ame_7_2_not_exists` and `ame_7_exists_iff` and every definition they use. Challenge.lean copies the definitions the statements use, and the two statements, verbatim, with Formal Conjectures' names; AME7/Defs.lean copies the file up to its benchmark statements, with the `category` and `AMS` attributes removed and Mathlib imported in place of Formal Conjectures' own library. In both, one proof step inside combineFirst is `exact Nat.sub_lt_sub_right him i.2` instead of Formal Conjectures' `omega` (see fidelity); audit/Audit.lean keeps Formal Conjectures' original under another name and checks by rfl that the two are equal. scripts/check-fc-match.py checks all of this against Formal Conjectures at that commit. Earlier versions of these proofs depended on Formal Conjectures directly (commit 9833012f) and were linked from Formal Conjectures PRs #7586 and #7611.",
